1
00:00:00,261 --> 00:00:02,671
Last video ended on a count that doubles

2
00:00:02,812 --> 00:00:04,560
every hour, two to the x.

3
00:00:05,323 --> 00:00:07,330
Money can double too, just more slowly.

4
00:00:07,974 --> 00:00:10,083
Put a thousand dollars into a savings account

5
00:00:10,165 --> 00:00:11,711
that doubles every ten years.

6
00:00:12,315 --> 00:00:14,440
Count in thousands of dollars and in decades,

7
00:00:14,842 --> 00:00:16,685
and the balance is two to the x.

8
00:00:17,389 --> 00:00:18,997
Here it is beside e to the x.

9
00:00:19,601 --> 00:00:20,705
Both start at a height of one.

10
00:00:21,710 --> 00:00:23,453
E to the x leaves that point with

11
00:00:23,494 --> 00:00:25,999
a slope of exactly one, because it's its

12
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:26,761
own derivative.

13
00:00:27,323 --> 00:00:29,260
But two to the x is flatter there.

14
00:00:29,885 --> 00:00:31,493
So the derivative of two to the x

15
00:00:31,755 --> 00:00:33,242
can't just be two to the x.

16
00:00:34,026 --> 00:00:36,524
Then how fast is the balance really growing?

17
00:00:37,172 --> 00:00:37,981
Here's the strange part.

18
00:00:38,447 --> 00:00:40,455
The answer contains a logarithm.

19
00:00:41,059 --> 00:00:42,406
Why would a log turn up when you

20
00:00:42,448 --> 00:00:43,896
differentiate an exponential?

21
00:00:44,730 --> 00:00:46,847
Last video gave us a measuring stick.

22
00:00:47,332 --> 00:00:49,005
Divide the gradient by the height.

23
00:00:49,832 --> 00:00:51,838
For e to the x, that ratio is

24
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:52,420
always one.

25
00:00:53,406 --> 00:00:55,134
Squash the curve to e to the two

26
00:00:55,295 --> 00:00:57,425
x, and the ratio is always two.

27
00:00:58,469 --> 00:01:01,134
Whenever the power is some number times x,

28
00:01:01,576 --> 00:01:03,920
the gradient is that number times the height.

29
00:01:04,524 --> 00:01:06,478
So the ratio tells you the number in

30
00:01:06,519 --> 00:01:06,982
the power.

31
00:01:07,808 --> 00:01:09,679
Let's measure two to the x that way.

32
00:01:11,069 --> 00:01:13,504
Start at x equals zero, where the height

33
00:01:13,626 --> 00:01:14,007
is one.

34
00:01:14,730 --> 00:01:17,233
Slide a second point in towards it, and

35
00:01:17,254 --> 00:01:18,855
the secant's slope settles:

36
00:01:19,497 --> 00:01:21,679
point eight three, point seven two,

37
00:01:22,201 --> 00:01:23,302
point six nine six.

38
00:01:24,105 --> 00:01:26,431
The tangent's slope is about point six nine

39
00:01:26,513 --> 00:01:26,732
three.

40
00:01:27,621 --> 00:01:28,392
Now move along.

41
00:01:28,997 --> 00:01:31,481
At x equals one, the height is two,

42
00:01:32,003 --> 00:01:33,986
and the gradient is about one point three

43
00:01:34,047 --> 00:01:34,327
nine.

44
00:01:35,110 --> 00:01:37,298
At x equals two, the height is four,

45
00:01:37,661 --> 00:01:39,608
and the gradient is about two point seven

46
00:01:39,669 --> 00:01:39,929
seven.

47
00:01:40,653 --> 00:01:43,040
The gradient is always the same fraction of

48
00:01:43,082 --> 00:01:43,462
the height.

49
00:01:44,026 --> 00:01:46,481
The ratio stays at point six nine three.

50
00:01:47,106 --> 00:01:49,116
That's the pattern we saw for e to

51
00:01:49,137 --> 00:01:50,403
a number times x.

52
00:01:51,161 --> 00:01:52,328
Try three to the x.

53
00:01:53,051 --> 00:01:55,256
Now the ratio settles at about one point

54
00:01:55,316 --> 00:01:58,123
zero nine nine, the same at every point.

55
00:01:58,946 --> 00:02:01,443
So each base has its own fixed ratio.

56
00:02:02,127 --> 00:02:04,615
Two gives about point six nine, three gives

57
00:02:04,655 --> 00:02:05,638
about one point one.

58
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:08,905
Somewhere between two and three, there must be

59
00:02:08,945 --> 00:02:11,170
a base with a ratio of exactly one.

60
00:02:12,114 --> 00:02:14,044
Slide the base from two up to three,

61
00:02:14,467 --> 00:02:15,693
and watch the ratio climb.

62
00:02:16,397 --> 00:02:18,564
At two point seven one eight, it reads

63
00:02:18,886 --> 00:02:19,026
one,

64
00:02:19,568 --> 00:02:21,474
and the curve lands right on top of

65
00:02:21,495 --> 00:02:22,297
e to the x.

66
00:02:22,922 --> 00:02:24,214
That base is e.

67
00:02:25,244 --> 00:02:26,315
So what are these numbers?

68
00:02:27,042 --> 00:02:28,971
Plot each ratio against its base.

69
00:02:29,514 --> 00:02:31,282
Two gives point six nine three.

70
00:02:31,986 --> 00:02:32,719
E gives one.

71
00:02:33,246 --> 00:02:36,017
Three gives one point zero nine nine, and

72
00:02:36,138 --> 00:02:38,166
four gives one point three eight six.

73
00:02:38,889 --> 00:02:40,613
These points sit on a curve you met

74
00:02:40,673 --> 00:02:42,960
in Year 11, the natural log curve.

75
00:02:43,665 --> 00:02:44,598
Check it on a calculator.

76
00:02:44,944 --> 00:02:47,199
The natural log of two is point six

77
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:47,742
nine three.

78
00:02:48,327 --> 00:02:50,153
So the gradient of a to the x

79
00:02:50,536 --> 00:02:52,945
is always the natural log of a, times

80
00:02:52,986 --> 00:02:53,346
the height.

81
00:02:53,950 --> 00:02:55,858
But why would a logarithm be the answer?

82
00:02:56,521 --> 00:02:57,866
The key is to write two as a

83
00:02:57,927 --> 00:02:58,429
power of e.

84
00:02:59,452 --> 00:03:01,117
The natural log of two is the power

85
00:03:01,137 --> 00:03:02,742
you raise e to, to get two.

86
00:03:03,303 --> 00:03:05,851
So two is approximately e to the point

87
00:03:05,892 --> 00:03:06,574
six nine three.

88
00:03:07,437 --> 00:03:10,007
Exactly, two to the x is e raised

89
00:03:10,047 --> 00:03:11,994
to the power x times the natural log

90
00:03:12,014 --> 00:03:12,356
of two.

91
00:03:13,059 --> 00:03:14,643
So two to the x is just e

92
00:03:14,985 --> 00:03:16,648
to the x, stretched sideways.

93
00:03:17,632 --> 00:03:19,537
Watch this tangent triangle on e to the

94
00:03:19,658 --> 00:03:20,760
x, at height two.

95
00:03:21,604 --> 00:03:23,508
Stretch it sideways by a factor of one

96
00:03:23,549 --> 00:03:25,874
point four four, and the run grows from

97
00:03:26,136 --> 00:03:28,301
one to one point four four, while the

98
00:03:28,382 --> 00:03:29,584
rise stays two.

99
00:03:30,326 --> 00:03:33,030
So at every height, the slope is multiplied

100
00:03:33,071 --> 00:03:34,452
by point six nine three,

101
00:03:35,054 --> 00:03:37,157
and the gradient becomes point six nine three

102
00:03:37,278 --> 00:03:37,998
times the height.

103
00:03:38,976 --> 00:03:41,330
Now let's prove it for any positive base

104
00:03:41,552 --> 00:03:41,652
a.

105
00:03:42,296 --> 00:03:44,261
The natural log of a is the power

106
00:03:44,302 --> 00:03:47,691
that turns e into a, so a equals

107
00:03:47,913 --> 00:03:49,236
e to the natural log of a.

108
00:03:49,979 --> 00:03:52,047
So a to the x is e raised

109
00:03:52,088 --> 00:03:52,910
to a new power,

110
00:03:53,413 --> 00:03:54,978
x times the natural log of a.

111
00:03:55,702 --> 00:03:56,465
Call that power u.

112
00:03:57,571 --> 00:03:59,534
The base is fixed, so the natural log

113
00:03:59,575 --> 00:04:00,736
of a is just a number,

114
00:04:01,278 --> 00:04:03,100
and d u by d x is the

115
00:04:03,141 --> 00:04:03,982
natural log of a.

116
00:04:04,745 --> 00:04:06,931
And d y by d u is e

117
00:04:06,973 --> 00:04:07,333
to the u.

118
00:04:08,198 --> 00:04:09,545
The chain rule multiplies them.

119
00:04:10,189 --> 00:04:12,057
Put the power back, and that e to

120
00:04:12,078 --> 00:04:13,765
the u is a to the x again.

121
00:04:14,649 --> 00:04:16,496
So the derivative of a to the x

122
00:04:16,918 --> 00:04:19,186
is the natural log of a, times a

123
00:04:19,207 --> 00:04:19,668
to the x.

124
00:04:20,473 --> 00:04:21,718
Try a equals e.

125
00:04:22,402 --> 00:04:24,426
The natural log of e is one, so

126
00:04:24,467 --> 00:04:26,150
you get e to the x back, the

127
00:04:26,191 --> 00:04:27,072
rule you already know.

128
00:04:27,801 --> 00:04:29,750
What if the base is less than two?

129
00:04:30,454 --> 00:04:31,140
Slide it down.

130
00:04:31,783 --> 00:04:34,152
At a equals one, the curve flattens into

131
00:04:34,192 --> 00:04:37,103
the line y equals one, with gradient zero.

132
00:04:37,746 --> 00:04:39,552
The rule agrees, because the natural log of

133
00:04:39,753 --> 00:04:40,576
one is zero.

134
00:04:41,319 --> 00:04:42,866
Keep going to a half.

135
00:04:43,570 --> 00:04:44,462
Now the curve falls.

136
00:04:45,050 --> 00:04:46,853
The natural log of a half is minus

137
00:04:46,894 --> 00:04:49,398
point six nine three, so the gradient is

138
00:04:49,559 --> 00:04:51,642
negative, while the height stays positive.

139
00:04:52,285 --> 00:04:54,088
A half to the x is two to

140
00:04:54,109 --> 00:04:56,353
the minus x, the mirror image of two

141
00:04:56,394 --> 00:04:56,854
to the x.

142
00:04:57,618 --> 00:04:59,105
And the base must be positive.

143
00:04:59,729 --> 00:05:02,012
The natural log of a negative number doesn't

144
00:05:02,053 --> 00:05:02,353
exist,

145
00:05:02,895 --> 00:05:04,838
and a negative base can't be raised to

146
00:05:04,939 --> 00:05:05,459
every power.

147
00:05:06,075 --> 00:05:08,720
Find the gradient of y equals two to

148
00:05:08,761 --> 00:05:10,624
the x at x equals three.

149
00:05:11,409 --> 00:05:12,694
Here the base is two.

150
00:05:13,317 --> 00:05:15,784
Copy two to the x, then multiply by

151
00:05:15,825 --> 00:05:17,108
the natural log of two.

152
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:19,373
So d y by d x is the

153
00:05:19,434 --> 00:05:21,598
natural log of two, times two to the

154
00:05:21,739 --> 00:05:21,818
x.

155
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:25,468
At x equals three, two cubed is eight,

156
00:05:25,830 --> 00:05:27,815
so the gradient is eight times the natural

157
00:05:27,856 --> 00:05:30,343
log of two, about five point five five.

158
00:05:31,046 --> 00:05:33,870
For the account, that's eight thousand dollars after

159
00:05:33,991 --> 00:05:36,214
thirty years, growing at about five and a

160
00:05:36,295 --> 00:05:37,837
half thousand dollars a decade.

161
00:05:38,659 --> 00:05:40,666
On the graph, the height is eight, and

162
00:05:40,687 --> 00:05:43,357
the gradient is point six nine three times

163
00:05:43,398 --> 00:05:43,578
that.

164
00:05:44,321 --> 00:05:46,007
If you wrote just two to the x,

165
00:05:46,289 --> 00:05:46,871
you'd get eight.

166
00:05:47,414 --> 00:05:48,945
That's the slope e to the x has

167
00:05:49,188 --> 00:05:49,711
at that height.

168
00:05:50,251 --> 00:05:51,202
Here's a way to remember it.

169
00:05:51,849 --> 00:05:53,211
Except when the base is one, a

170
00:05:53,934 --> 00:05:55,577
to the x is e to the x

171
00:05:55,759 --> 00:05:56,860
scaled sideways.

172
00:05:57,544 --> 00:05:59,270
The natural log of the base sets the

173
00:05:59,291 --> 00:05:59,592
scale.

174
00:06:00,299 --> 00:06:01,632
You can see that number on the graph.

175
00:06:02,217 --> 00:06:04,025
Where a to the x crosses the y

176
00:06:04,126 --> 00:06:05,894
axis, its height is one.

177
00:06:06,619 --> 00:06:08,710
So its slope there is exactly the natural

178
00:06:08,771 --> 00:06:09,253
log of a.

179
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:12,224
Two to the x leaves with slope point

180
00:06:12,285 --> 00:06:13,066
six nine three,

181
00:06:13,829 --> 00:06:15,512
and e to the x with slope one.

182
00:06:16,295 --> 00:06:18,841
So copy the exponential, then multiply by the

183
00:06:18,923 --> 00:06:20,145
natural log of the base.

184
00:06:22,858 --> 00:06:23,322
Your turn.

185
00:06:23,785 --> 00:06:25,748
For f of x equals five to the

186
00:06:25,930 --> 00:06:28,714
x, find f prime of x, then the

187
00:06:28,795 --> 00:06:31,219
exact value of f prime of zero.

188
00:06:31,783 --> 00:06:32,690
Pause here to answer.

189
00:06:43,435 --> 00:06:46,024
The base is five, so f prime of

190
00:06:46,085 --> 00:06:48,433
x is the natural log of five, times

191
00:06:48,495 --> 00:06:49,237
five to the x.

192
00:06:50,020 --> 00:06:50,540
At zero,

193
00:06:51,082 --> 00:06:53,346
five to the zero is one, so f

194
00:06:53,387 --> 00:06:55,911
prime of zero is exactly the natural log

195
00:06:55,952 --> 00:06:57,875
of five, about one point six one.

196
00:06:58,738 --> 00:07:00,480
If you wrote x times five to the

197
00:07:00,582 --> 00:07:03,327
x minus one, that's the power rule, and

198
00:07:03,388 --> 00:07:04,429
it needs x in the base.

199
00:07:05,052 --> 00:07:07,226
It gives zero here, a flat tangent on

200
00:07:07,247 --> 00:07:07,991
a rising curve.

201
00:07:09,482 --> 00:07:09,866
Last one.

202
00:07:10,411 --> 00:07:12,593
For g of x equals a half to

203
00:07:12,613 --> 00:07:15,515
the x, find the exact value of g

204
00:07:15,575 --> 00:07:18,297
prime of two, and explain its sign.

205
00:07:18,981 --> 00:07:19,874
Pause here to answer.

206
00:07:30,528 --> 00:07:32,632
G prime of x is the natural log

207
00:07:32,673 --> 00:07:34,777
of a half, times a half to the

208
00:07:34,999 --> 00:07:35,138
x.

209
00:07:36,061 --> 00:07:38,062
At two, a half squared is a quarter,

210
00:07:38,483 --> 00:07:40,704
so g prime of two is a quarter

211
00:07:40,905 --> 00:07:43,006
of the natural log of a half, which

212
00:07:43,067 --> 00:07:45,367
is minus the natural log of two, over

213
00:07:45,428 --> 00:07:45,688
four.

214
00:07:46,409 --> 00:07:48,430
It's negative because the base is less than

215
00:07:48,651 --> 00:07:51,332
one, so its natural log is negative, while

216
00:07:51,373 --> 00:07:53,113
a half to the x is always positive.

217
00:07:53,815 --> 00:07:55,641
Writing the natural log of two there gives

218
00:07:55,683 --> 00:07:56,425
the wrong sign.

219
00:07:58,147 --> 00:07:59,869
So a to the x is e with

220
00:08:00,130 --> 00:08:01,891
x times the natural log of a in

221
00:08:01,912 --> 00:08:02,352
the power,

222
00:08:02,873 --> 00:08:04,554
and its derivative is the natural log of

223
00:08:04,575 --> 00:08:06,296
a, times a to the x.

224
00:08:07,340 --> 00:08:07,580
Next:

225
00:08:08,183 --> 00:08:10,490
our ratio points traced the natural log curve.

226
00:08:11,214 --> 00:08:13,064
What's the gradient of that curve itself?

227
00:08:15,761 --> 00:08:16,625
Here are the key notes.

228
00:08:17,027 --> 00:08:18,575
Pause the video if you need more time

229
00:08:18,616 --> 00:08:19,078
to copy them.
